{
  "id": "choose-a-visualization-read-a-table", "title": "Read row-level detail",
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You'll follow one table row across fields instead of reducing it to a single number or shape." },
    { "type": "section", "id": "read-table", "title": "Read a record across columns", "blocks": [
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "navigate", "reftarget": "/d/OhR1ID6Mk/table?viewPanel=12&from=now-1h&to=now&timezone=browser", "verify": "on-page:/d/OhR1ID6Mk", "content": "Open **Image cell and bar gauge cell** on the **Table** dashboard." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Find the row with **id** 1. Follow that row to **Catch phrase** and read its text. Notice how the column headings tell you what each cell means." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Move across the table to inspect **Something** and **Sensor**, scrolling horizontally if needed. The same record includes text and a numeric sensor value. Images and bar gauge cells format fields without turning the whole table into a chart." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Choose a table when the viewer needs exact values or several fields from each record. Tables can show more than one query result; if a dataset selector is present, identify the selected result before comparing rows." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Match the question to the display: one value uses a stat; position within a range uses a gauge or bar gauge; category comparison uses bars; share of an included total uses a pie; record-level detail uses a table." }
    ] },
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You've used each visualization from slides 2 and 3 for a different reading task. Continue with time series when the question asks how values change over time." }
  ]
}